faqs:
  - q: "How long does a HubSpot audit take?"
    a: "It depends on the size of the portal, the number of hubs and integrations, and how much automation has built up. On our projects, audit and architecture together typically take one to two weeks. A focused audit of a single area, such as data quality, can be shorter."
  - q: "What do I get at the end of a HubSpot audit?"
    a: "A written findings document: what is working, what is broken, and what each problem is costing in time or trust, with recommendations ordered by priority. A good audit ends with a plan you can act on yourself or hand to a partner."
  - q: "Does audit work carry into a rebuild?"
    a: "It should. The audit is the discovery stage of a rebuild, so the findings become the brief for the architecture. When we run an audit and the client goes ahead with the build, the audit work carries into it rather than being repeated."
  - q: "How often should a HubSpot portal be audited?"
    a: "Run a full audit when you inherit a portal, before a migration or rebuild, and when reports start to disagree. Between those, a short quarterly review of duplicates, unused properties, failing workflows and sync errors catches most problems before they grow."
